<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="0.4" dur="4.4">Uh so, what happened? Right? I&amp;#39;ve heard</text><text start="2.4" dur="5.2">a lot of the rumors like Mark Wayne has.</text><text start="4.8" dur="4.8">Uh but uh what we have is an incredibly</text><text start="7.6" dur="5">old air traffic control system. I think</text><text start="9.6" dur="5.7">every single one of your networks have</text><text start="12.6" dur="4.9">covered the president and myself talking</text><text start="15.3" dur="4.5">about this for the last two years. The</text><text start="17.5" dur="5.1">president for the last year has been</text><text start="19.8" dur="4.9">asking Congress to fully fund</text><text start="22.6" dur="3.8">uh a full build of a brand new air</text><text start="24.7" dur="4.9">traffic control system.</text><text start="26.4" dur="6.7">So, we have TDM uh telecom. So, this is</text><text start="29.6" dur="5.6">analog telecom. Our switches, uh our</text><text start="33.1" dur="3">routers actually got overloaded with</text><text start="35.2" dur="2.2">data</text><text start="36.1" dur="3.2">and they went down.</text><text start="37.4" dur="3.9">And uh I shouldn&amp;#39;t say they went down.</text><text start="39.3" dur="3.1">They started to give us inconsistency in</text><text start="41.3" dur="3.9">the data</text><text start="42.4" dur="4.2">uh from those uh from those routers. And</text><text start="45.2" dur="2.3">because of that, we shut the system</text><text start="46.6" dur="3.1">down.</text><text start="47.5" dur="4.3">Now, I I have already replaced some of</text><text start="49.7" dur="4.8">those switches with President Trump. And</text><text start="51.8" dur="5.6">our new IP switches did not go down.</text><text start="54.5" dur="4">It&amp;#39;s the old hardware uh that went down.</text><text start="57.4" dur="3.8">And I think the question for the</text><text start="58.5" dur="4.9">American people is</text><text start="61.2" dur="4.9">do you want your Congress to fund this?</text><text start="63.4" dur="4.2">President Trump has asked for the money.</text><text start="66.1" dur="5.1">Uh he&amp;#39;s asked the Congress on a</text><text start="67.6" dur="5.4">bipartisan uh uh approach to say give us</text><text start="71.2" dur="3.4">the resources to build a</text><text start="73" dur="5.2">state-of-the-art air traffic control</text><text start="74.6" dur="6.3">system. Let&amp;#39;s not do a patchwork uh uh</text><text start="78.2" dur="4.3">uh fix to a system that&amp;#39;s critical for</text><text start="80.9" dur="2.9">every single family. It&amp;#39;s not red, it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="82.5" dur="4.2">not blue, it&amp;#39;s not Democrat, it&amp;#39;s not</text><text start="83.8" dur="5">Republican. It&amp;#39;s American. Give us the</text><text start="86.7" dur="4.2">money to fix it. Now, if you look to the</text><text start="88.8" dur="5.6">past administrations, going back 25</text><text start="90.9" dur="6.1">years, uh $15 billion</text><text start="94.4" dur="4.7">has been given to the FAA to fix this</text><text start="97" dur="4.9">air traffic control system. And guess</text><text start="99.1" dur="4.9">what? Barely anything was done.</text><text start="101.9" dur="3.9">We had a down payment. Uh President</text><text start="104" dur="4.6">Trump asked for it in the uh one big</text><text start="105.8" dur="5.4">beautiful bill of $12.5 billion.</text><text start="108.6" dur="4.9">We are building in that $12.5 billion,</text><text start="111.2" dur="3.6">that portion of the build will be done</text><text start="113.5" dur="3.3">by the time President Trump leaves</text><text start="114.8" dur="4.2">office. We are moving at a speed that</text><text start="116.8" dur="4.292">has never uh been seen before with</text><text start="119" dur="4.892">regard to FAA.</text><text start="121.092" dur="4.2">But uh that&amp;#39;s a partial funding.</text><text start="123.892" dur="4.1">I think America demands that the</text><text start="125.292" dur="7">Congress give the rest of the resources</text><text start="127.992" dur="6.3">to finish the bill. Um and</text><text start="132.292" dur="3.4">I think the Congress at a point</text><text start="134.292" dur="3.5">looked to the history of the FAA and</text><text start="135.692" dur="4">said we don&amp;#39;t trust you.</text><text start="137.792" dur="4.4">Well, with President Trump and what</text><text start="139.692" dur="4.6">we&amp;#39;ve done, I think they do trust</text><text start="142.192" dur="3.7">because what we&amp;#39;ve done with that first</text><text start="144.292" dur="3.5">tranche of money.</text><text start="145.892" dur="3.4">And so uh with a brand new</text><text start="147.792" dur="3.6">state-of-the-art system, you won&amp;#39;t have</text><text start="149.292" dur="3.4">these outages. So what you experienced</text><text start="151.392" dur="3">today, but you can think back, many of</text><text start="152.692" dur="3.5">you covered the story from a year and a</text><text start="154.392" dur="3.7">half ago, we had outages in Newark,</text><text start="156.192" dur="5.2">multiple outages in Newark.</text><text start="158.092" dur="6.5">This is a continual problem that we have</text><text start="161.392" dur="6.2">um and it should be fixed. Um and so</text><text start="164.592" dur="5.3">what we want to do um I&amp;#39;ve asked the</text><text start="167.592" dur="3.8">president&amp;#39;s asked for $30 billion.</text><text start="169.892" dur="2.4">I want $50 billion.</text><text start="171.392" dur="2.7">And by the way, if you look at how much</text><text start="172.292" dur="4.1">money Congress spends, Peter, you&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="174.092" dur="4.3">covered Congress, they they waste a lot</text><text start="176.392" dur="3.5">of money. What&amp;#39;s more important than</text><text start="178.392" dur="3.2">having an air traffic control system</text><text start="179.892" dur="2.8">that actually works?</text><text start="181.592" dur="4.3">And so the president said, you know</text><text start="182.692" dur="5.8">what? Let&amp;#39;s finish this job. New</text><text start="185.892" dur="4.2">hardware, new software, new</text><text start="188.492" dur="3.8">telecommunication.</text><text start="190.092" dur="3.4">Uh many of our towers are almost 100</text><text start="192.292" dur="3">years old.</text><text start="193.492" dur="3.2">Uh our our air traffic controllers have</text><text start="195.292" dur="3">leaky roofs, air conditioning that</text><text start="196.692" dur="3.6">doesn&amp;#39;t work. They&amp;#39;re high in the air,</text><text start="198.292" dur="5.1">their elevators don&amp;#39;t work. Their roofs</text><text start="200.292" dur="5.4">leak. Um I want new towers. Uh we should</text><text start="203.392" dur="4.8">also invest in many of the airports</text><text start="205.692" dur="4.4">around the country uh that frankly many</text><text start="208.192" dur="4.4">of them are embarrassing. Let&amp;#39;s get the</text><text start="210.092" dur="4.3">money. Let&amp;#39;s invest so we never have to</text><text start="212.592" dur="3.7">come at</text><text start="214.392" dur="4.2">8:30 at night and have a press</text><text start="216.292" dur="3.8">conference on why air travel was shut</text><text start="218.592" dur="3.7">down, why we have</text><text start="220.092" dur="4.3">tens of thousands of people in airports</text><text start="222.292" dur="4.8">uh separated from their families uh</text><text start="224.392" dur="4.4">without um with without uh any knowledge</text><text start="227.092" dur="3.6">of where they&amp;#39;re going to sleep tonight.</text><text start="228.792" dur="4.4">Now you probably picked up that uh we</text><text start="230.692" dur="4">how we&amp;#39;ve I identified the problem.</text><text start="233.192" dur="3.4">We&amp;#39;ve got our centers and our TRACONs</text><text start="234.692" dur="5">operational right now.</text><text start="236.592" dur="5.4">And so at 8:15 tonight uh Eastern time,</text><text start="239.692" dur="4.202">we&amp;#39;ve opened up the airspace. Now does</text><text start="241.992" dur="3.002">that mean every flight is going to fly</text><text start="243.894" dur="3.1">right now?</text><text start="244.994" dur="3.5">It&amp;#39;s It&amp;#39;s going to be slow, right? So,</text><text start="246.994" dur="4.4">if if you&amp;#39;re watching, you&amp;#39;re at an</text><text start="248.494" dur="4.2">airport, um check with your airline. Uh</text><text start="251.394" dur="3.7">it depends on do we have crews</text><text start="252.694" dur="4.2">available? Uh do we have pilots and</text><text start="255.094" dur="2.7">flight attendants available to fly your</text><text start="256.894" dur="3.5">flight? We&amp;#39;re going to try to move as</text><text start="257.794" dur="4.7">many of those as we can tonight if we</text><text start="260.394" dur="4.1">have the capacity with crews to to to</text><text start="262.494" dur="3.8">move those flights. If not, we&amp;#39;re going</text><text start="264.494" dur="4.4">to uh start tomorrow morning with our</text><text start="266.294" dur="5">airline partners um moving those</text><text start="268.894" dur="2.4">aircraft.</text></transcript>